# Files that are not pages. The repository root is the web root, so anything
# committed here is a URL unless it is kept out of the deployment.
#
# vercel.json answers these paths with 404, but a `routes` rule with a status
# and no dest only rewrites the status line: Vercel still sent the whole file
# body under it. Verified after the deploy of 9217a17:
#
#   /posts/postgres-copied-5gb-before-recovery-started.md  404, 11020 bytes
#   /scripts/verify_links.py                               404, 16186 bytes
#
# So the exclusion has to happen before the upload, not at request time. The
# vercel.json rule stays as the second line of defence, and as the thing that
# still answers 404 for a path that is ignored here but cached at the edge.

scripts/
.github/
*.md
*.py
*.yaml
*.yml
